@page "/AboutUs"
@using MudBlazor.Charts

<PageTitle>About Us</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Large" Class="mt-6 mb-10">

  <h1 class="mb-2">About Backstage</h1>

<MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6">
    <h3>What is Backstage?</h3>

    <p>Backstage is the inventory management and organizational platform
         for the Chicago International Puppet Theater Festival.</p>

    @* <h3  class="mt-4">The Problem</h3>

    <p>Relying on dated spreadsheets and group chats to track merchandise
        quantity and location can be inefficient during a busy festival season.
        The Puppet Festival needed a centralized system to accurately manage
        inventory, locations, and merchandise availability in real time.
    </p> *@


</MudPaper>
    <h2 class="mb-2">Core Features</h2>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6">
       <MudList T="string" Dense="true">
    <MudListItem>Alerts - View low-stock and out-of-stock alerts per location.</MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Product Catalog - Create and view festival merchandise.</MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Inventory - Track and update inventory quantities by location.</MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Locations - Create and view locations, including theaters and vans, where merchandise is stored and/or sold at. </MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Pack a Box + Outgoing/Incoming Boxes - Create and pack boxes to be picked up and transported to different locations.</MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Sales - Record sales as they happen to update the inventory at a location in real-time. </MudListItem>
    <MudListItem>Inventory Recount - Adjust inventory in bulk to reflect untracked sales and ensure quantities are accurate at the end of the night.</MudListItem>
</MudList>
    </MudPaper>

    <h2 class="mb-2">How To Use Backstage</h2>

    <h3>Sales Staff</h3>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6" >
        <ol  style="padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Login to access the dashboard and management tools.</li>
            <li>Use the sidebar to navigate the platform. Refer to "Core Features" above for more detailed descriptions of each page's use.</li>
            <li>Recording a sale in "Sales" to update inventory or update all inventory manually in "Inventory Recount"</li>
        </ol>
    </MudPaper>

    <h3>Inventory Manager</h3>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6" >
        <ol  style="padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Everything from Sales Staff above and:</li>
            <li>View low-stock and out-of-stock alerts per location in "Alerts".</li>
            <li>Using the "Alerts" page, create and pack boxes to be picked up and transported to different locations in "Pack a Box".</li>
            <li>View, update, and create new festival merchandise items in "Product Catalog".</li>
        </ol>
    </MudPaper>

    <h3>Admin</h3>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6" >
        <ol  style="padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Everything as from Inventory Manager above and:</li>
            <li>View and create/update locations for the festival, (theaters or vans) in "Locations".</li>
            <li>View where merchandise is going or if it has arrived in "Outgoing/Incoming Boxes".</li>
            <li>Add new users and manage their permissions in "Admin User Management".</li>
        </ol>
    </MudPaper>

    <h3>Van Driver</h3>

    <MudPaper Class="pa-6 mb-6" >
        <ol  style="padding-left: 20px;">
            <li>Login to access the dashboard and management tools.</li>
            <li>Use the sidebar to navigate the platform. Refer to "Core Features" above for more detailed descriptions of each page's use.</li>
            <li>View current deliveries in "Outgoing/Incoming Boxes".</li>
        </ol>
    </MudPaper>

